    <div class="prose-linen text-lg md:col-span-4 md:col-start-9">
      <p>Each room is named after a dye the Vásquez family once boiled in the courtyard's basins: the red of cochineal, the blue of indigo, the gold of marigold, the brown of walnut husks, and the roof room left undyed.</p>
      <p>The sheets, the blankets and the curtains come from the Bautista looms in Teotitlán del Valle, where Inés grew up, woven for each room in its own color.</p>
